# Robotics 2: Dynamics

Forces and motion. This chapter relates the joint torques of a robot to the accelerations they produce: the torques a planned motion needs, the inertia matrix and the velocity and gravity forces that make up the equations of motion, the accelerations under given torques, and the energies, which a simulation must conserve.

- [Inverse dynamics](robot_02_dynamics/torques.md)
- [Mass matrix and simulation](robot_02_dynamics/mass_matrix_and_simulation.md)
